Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:36:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?asteroids:=20OPTIONAL=20=E2=80=94=20disable=20S?=
 =?UTF-8?q?UPL=20(AGPS)=20to=20stop=20GPS=20phoning=20supl.google.com?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Blank gps.supl_host for the default carrier so the GPS HAL uses
standalone mode instead of assisted GPS.

Privacy: SUPL sends a cell-tower-derived location estimate to
supl.google.com on GPS requests. Disabling it keeps GPS fixes entirely
local (no Google round-trip).

Tradeoff: cold GPS lock is slower (tens of seconds to ~2 min without
assistance) and first-fix-in-doors may be degraded. Emergency services
location is unaffected (E911 uses control-plane, not SUPL).

NOT included in the main series — apply only if you accept the tradeoff.
Revert by restoring <string name="gps.supl_host">supl.google.com</string>.

Note: the Japanese carrier block still sets supl.rm-n.jp; blank those too
if you roam on that carrier.
---
 rro_overlays/CarrierConfigResCommon_Vendor/res/xml/vendor.xml | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rro_overlays/CarrierConfigResCommon_Vendor/res/xml/vendor.xml b/rro_overlays/CarrierConfigResCommon_Vendor/res/xml/vendor.xml
index 251fea2..afc2da1 100644
--- a/rro_overlays/CarrierConfigResCommon_Vendor/res/xml/vendor.xml
+++ b/rro_overlays/CarrierConfigResCommon_Vendor/res/xml/vendor.xml
@@ -38,7 +38,8 @@
         <string name="gps.a_glonass_pos_protocol_select">15</string>
         <string name="gps.lpp_profile">15</string>
         <string name="gps.nfw_proxy_apps">com.example.android.locationattribution</string>
-        <string name="gps.supl_host">supl.google.com</string>
+        <!-- lenOS (OPTIONAL privacy): SUPL disabled -> GPS uses standalone (no location leak to Google). Tradeoff: slower cold GPS lock. Revert this line to re-enable AGPS. -->
+        <string name="gps.supl_host"></string>
         <string name="gps.supl_port">7275</string>
         <string name="gps.supl_ver">0x20004</string>
         <boolean name="hide_enable_2g_bool" value="true" />
